{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557210-my-tattered-facade-view","id":1557210,"title":"My Tattered Facade view.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-02T12:13:42-08:00","id":1557210,"title":"My Tattered Facade view.","content":"The other day I picked up VTM Tattered Facade sourcebook and I found it a useful addition to my collection as it gives more ideas on what kind of nightly horror a &quot;typical&quot; kindred would have and how hard it is to maintain the Masquerade and what sort of people you would encounter during the night when most of us would be in bed asleep.<br /> <br /> There's is some helpful storytelling ideas and they come up with more clan archetypes and what sort of skills and disciplines that would be fitting. Not to mention what type of struggles that each clan would have and some story ideas and I personally liked the Collector archetype for the Tzmisce the most with the Ventrue Headhunter and Ministry Procurer archetypes a close second and third.<br /> <br /> They do have some neat new and darker discipline abilities and amalgams and a set of new lore sheets. I should mention that they have a section on what kind of horror vibes that you can work with from gothic horror to eldritch themes that would fit in a H.P. Lovecraft setting.<br /> <br /> All in all, I found it a good addition to my collection of VTM books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 01-03-2026, 11:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-02T13:05:45-08:00","id":1557211,"title":"","content":"What did you think of the Baali and the Ghuls?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-02T19:01:15-08:00","id":1557220,"title":"","content":"In general a good book, but did they truly had to utterly retcon the baali?<br /> <br /> There' s not even a pretense of respecting previous lore now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-02T21:42:03-08:00","id":1557221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557210-my-tattered-facade-view?p=1557211#post1557211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did you think of the Baali and the Ghuls?</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked what they did to them, the Baali are more tolerable as I never liked them as a bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-02T23:01:19-08:00","id":1557222,"title":"","content":"What did they do to the Baali?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-02T23:16:43-08:00","id":1557223,"title":"","content":"They made the Baali into a group of possessed kindred that have lost all semblance of humanity but still have intelligence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T01:53:21-08:00","id":1557224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557210-my-tattered-facade-view?p=1557222#post1557222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did they do to the Baali?</div> </div> </div> </div>To quote from the book (pg. 142):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since the earliest days of Sumer, Kindred Blood Sorcerers have tried to recapture the powers of Enoch and their progenitors by summoning, questioning,<br /> and communing with the aapilum (Akkadian for \u201cthe ones who answer\u201d; see Aapilu, p. 141), entities latent within the sorcerer\u2019s Blood lineage. When such communion becomes possession, the reflection (abaalu in Akkadian) and the original merge. The result is one of the Baali. Some Kindred scholars consider them a type of wight, though one with a seemingly intact intellect. </div> </div> </div>So that's this book's take on Baali. Right now with Renegade books, you can pretty much get everything: A continuation of old lore, retcons of old lore or completely new lore. But when you get what of these on any point is inconsistent and feels somewhat random. Like in this case: Previously, V5 has studiously avoided introducing the Baali to V5 but now they're back... except it's not the Baali from the old lore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T13:40:36-08:00","id":1557242,"title":"","content":"Wow. They somehow managed to introduce a fourth, LEAST INTERESTING version of the Baali. And in a way that removes the previous versions as considerations.<br /> <br /> I assume the current writers are not interested in really exploring Infernalism, hence &quot;Baali are just Wights, but Smart&quot;. But it makes the entire Bloodline so much less useful, compared to...well, any of its previous incarnations. Much less &quot;multiple different expressions of the same Bloodline, but with diametrically different goals&quot; of V20.<br /> <br /> SMDH.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-03T21:14:26-08:00","id":1557252,"title":"","content":"You realize that you can tweak the Baali in your games and don't need to follow the metaplot word for word?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T08:36:40-08:00","id":1557258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557210-my-tattered-facade-view?p=1557252#post1557252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You realize that you can tweak the Baali in your games and don't need to follow the metaplot word for word?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Please, let's not use the golden rule as an excuse for bad choices in writing. <br /> <br /> The entire point of this being a 5th edition of a decades old games rather than a reboot is that it is the same universe as previous edition. <br /> <br /> Which means baali should be what they've always been, not the latest idea of writers more than 20 years after the baali's original conception. <br /> <br /> There was no point in doing what they did except to reject past continuity. <br /> <br /> What stopped the authors from creating a new concept of vampire sorcerers possessed by these blood borne entities rather than hijack the baali? <br /> <br /> <br /> That's the entire problem with the 5th editions. If the goal is to do your own thing and not respect decades of past lore, why call it a 5th edition? Why not do as Kult did and embrace that divinity lost is a reboot and not &quot;kult:4th Ed&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T09:53:08-08:00","id":1557261,"title":"","content":"Let's not pretend that VTM didn't retcon characters and storyline lore in there entire run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T10:33:00-08:00","id":1557262,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24043\" data-vbnamecard=\"24043\">Nyremne</a> Because they don't have any original ideas for themselves. Now, that's not to say you can NEVER build upon an idea someone else already made, but if you are going to do so, do it as an honest continuation of characterization / plot. The Paradox-Renegade paradigm of White Wolf needs the brand recognition of Classic World of Darkness to bare profitability, but they don't care about the actual lovingly made lore and it distinctly shows.<br /> <br /> Same reason why they didn't do all this nonsense under CofD and soft-discontinued it: it never had the same cultural impact or &quot;brand recognition&quot; as cWoD did. Which I found bizarre that they didn't just utilize CofD, because that's the line explicitly meant to be more Metaplot-lite than cWoD.<br /> <br /> The most explicit of this cynical practice already has precedent in Reckoning, wherein the Imbued of all things, are nowhere to be found in their own gameline of all things. If they wanted generic hunters, they could have just made a Hunter's Hunted 3 / &quot;X5&quot;; but of course, they didn't, for the reasons we know why.<br /> <br /> They have (presumably) all the past book material at their disposal; they can easily read the past work and get paid the privilege to do that as a means of their work; but ultimately don't care because they (most likely) think what they're writing is &quot;better&quot; or more digestible than the past writers for so-called &quot;newer&quot; audiences... when in actuality all they're doing is churning out low-quality drivel writing and introducing elementary retcon-based plot points that aren't really at par with the 90s era writing (as much as many for whatever reason deride it, myself saying that as so-called &quot;Gen Z&quot;).<br /> <br /> Of course, that is not to say the past writing was perfect, with many major and minor gripes I have myself, but it was vastly way more coherent and gripping than what V5 and beyond is doing.<br /> <br /> This retcon of the Baali in this &quot;Tattered Facade&quot; is the most indicative of it. Instead of a bloodline (we also have to remember Paradox-Renegade hates bloodlines, too much complexity) spawned from the inadvertent primordial sin of the most thought of as serene, innocent in the face of vampirism, and Golconda-seeking Saulot; we get this low-stake trash of the Baali just being intelligent Wights of all things... Wights because Paths have been excised from the game from both an in-game and meta-perspective; and also Wights, because we wouldn't want players to actually play them (and yes, I know Baali players most likely are &quot;rare&quot;; but only in the sense of a GM allowing that to be played. At my tables, I'd certainly allow a secret Baali player just to keep things interesting.. but I'm aware most WoD GMs/STs aren't as talented.. not to toot my own horn much). More &quot;NPC&quot; only drivel like they did with the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Also, on the previous points I broached on, the Baali had to be deconstructed by Renegade because it was too much of a metaplot heavy bloodline. Off the top of my head: it was connected with Saulot, had influences with the destruction of Carthage, heavily infiltrated the Tremere along with the Camarilla proper and Sabbat at large, and most importantly, was able to literally cross-convert proper clan Kindred into the Baali bloodline; and from a gameplay, not only metaplot perspective, was able to summon non-DtF Demons (considering the Baali was conceived before the mess that was DtF.. but that within itself is a story for another time) to help them fight their battles or just outright manipulate humanity... Yeah, it was too complex for the minds at Paradox-Renegade.<br /> <br /> I don't support V5 products either way, so thanks for this review. I probably would've not known the Baali were retconned (again, since I believe even the past pre-V5 they were retconned) if not for it.<br /> <br /> The title of this book is poignant in a sense, because it certainly is a tattered facade of the World of Darkness..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T10:42:31-08:00","id":1557263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557210-my-tattered-facade-view?p=1557261#post1557261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not pretend that VTM didn't retcon characters and storyline lore in there entire run.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And when it did, it was called out. Retcon is one of the capital sins of writing.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;previous editions did a nad thing&quot; doesn't justify said bad thing in the present.<br /> That was the same bad argument given to justify the horrific layout of V5 corebook &quot;but vtm always had bad layout&quot;.<br /> <br /> Should the next books also lack content that will have to be in erratum in future ones because it happened in 1st and second edition? Should template characters be extremely ill balanced because there were ill balanced template char in previous editions?<br /> <br /> <br /> Or should the writers of now make quality products using decades of errors as a learning ground of what not to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T11:01:35-08:00","id":1557268,"title":"","content":"I'd actually say that not ALL retcons are bad, it's just that when (and IF) you have to retcon something; make it a REFINEMENT, instead of an ill-advised venture that only made things worse. The polemic problem most modern writers have nowadays, is an unfounded superiority against the past (which is found in SCORES with Paradox-Renegade; along with some of their fans with that mindset).<br /> <br /> In their heads they think they're crafting pure mastery, but when presented to audiences, it's just pure trash. Having an original idea is hard but so is continuing a good idea and trying to respect it. Lazy writers and/or bad writers implement without taking proper heed of past material, because it's an easier thing to accomplish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T11:01:40-08:00","id":1557269,"title":"","content":"And since we're on that issue, the baali exemple of this book show another issue of the V5 line. <br /> <br /> If we take away the nonsense that these entities are supposed to be baali, the notion that there are things born in the blood of vampires from the collective experiences of sires and absorbed blood from victims, that can be called through sorcery for power but risk taking over the sorcerer is a good one. <br /> <br /> But as always with V5 ideas, good or bad. They are, for the lck of a better word, dry. <br /> <br /> What I mean by that is that there's too little meat to it. That's the same for the notion of tiamat's veins, or thin blood alchemy, or most loresheets post corebook. <br /> <br /> These are presented as interesting tidbits, but their impact on the world are weak. <br /> <br /> Take the aapilu here. These are basically inner demons that you can summons, fgzin something from them in exchange for doing terrible acts. <br /> <br /> And there are three of them described in the book. Each ones whose pact is not particularly important compared to the efforts and risks needed to summon them. <br /> <br /> The whole point of infernalism is that even if you know it's a bad idea, the offer is utterly tempting. <br /> <br /> <br /> And that's the same all across V5. Tiamat's vein, this metaphor (or is it?) of the leylines of the world as veins of blood of a cosmic entities, whose intersection cause weird events, in a way finally deciding that there's no reasons vampires should be the only critters in the wod not interested in nodes and leylines, and what's the result? Rites that can tap in this leylines/cosmic monster.... For a few dices in addition to a roll. <br /> <br /> Thin blood alchemy, the birth of a new power at the edge between humanity and czinites, and it's just either copying low level disciplines or very circonstantial powers whose cost outmach their utility. <br /> <br /> Same for world shattering loresheets. I have access to the legendary tapestry of blood, for which two antedilucians fought each others, and the result? A few hints on immediate future events when studied. <br /> <br /> A loresheet about being connected to Beckett? A few dots in research or contacts. <br /> <br /> <br /> Everything interesting end up without impact, adding a few dice here or there. <br /> <br /> My personnal theory would be that the authors are deathly afraid that giving any meat to any of those would go into the &quot;gonzo&quot; territory they tried to shy away when making this edition. <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T11:07:38-08:00","id":1557272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1557210-my-tattered-facade-view?p=1557268#post1557268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd actually say that not ALL retcons are bad, it's just that when (and IF) you have to retcon something; make it a REFINEMENT, instead of an ill-advised venture that only made things worse. The polemic problem most modern writers have nowadays, is an unfounded superiority against the past (which is found in SCORES with Paradox-Renegade; along with some of their fans with that mindset).<br /> <br /> In their heads they think they're crafting pure mastery, but when presented to audiences, it's just pure trash. Having an original idea is hard but so is continuing a good idea and trying to respect it. Lazy writers and/or bad writers implement without taking proper heed of past material, because it's an easier thing to accomplish.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I understand your point, I'm more of the school of &quot; the only time retcon should be done is it's something that would add so much to the setting over a minor change, and the current way the lore is written don't allow any other way to implement that idea&quot; <br /> <br /> <br /> Which, to be fair is nearlybequivalent to me saying not retcon are justified, as I think that with enough good will and brain matter, all retcon can be avoided with careful thinking. The only places where I tolerate retcon are settings where there's multiple authors saying mutually exclusive things and later writers has the difficult task of deciding a Canon answer. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-04T19:13:02-08:00","id":1557292,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">This thread is in danger of going into Rule 3 territory. Please dial it back a bit. </span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}